\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Construction workflow for UrbanMobility-Instruct. Reasoning levels and instruction schemas guide grounded seed authoring, followed by concept-group identification, controlled augmentation, structural validation, task-view materialization, and partition auditing. A shared resolved concept-group map assigns all related records to the same partition. The lower panel illustrates a Level~1 multiple-choice seed grounded in highD. The identifiers \texttt  {highd\_l1\_spatial\_01} and \texttt  {highd\_spatial\_coverage} are illustrative rather than literal corpus identifiers; actual group identifiers follow the source-and-hash construction and alias resolution described below.}}{8}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:urban_llm_flowchart}{{1}{8}{Construction workflow for UrbanMobility-Instruct. Reasoning levels and instruction schemas guide grounded seed authoring, followed by concept-group identification, controlled augmentation, structural validation, task-view materialization, and partition auditing. A shared resolved concept-group map assigns all related records to the same partition. The lower panel illustrates a Level~1 multiple-choice seed grounded in highD. The identifiers \texttt {highd\_l1\_spatial\_01} and \texttt {highd\_spatial\_coverage} are illustrative rather than literal corpus identifiers; actual group identifiers follow the source-and-hash construction and alias resolution described below}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Primary-source corpus composition and training views. Panel~(a) shows 10,560 canonical records by source and reasoning level; panel~(b) shows MC/SA shares and their level composition; panel~(c) shows generation, verification, and paraphrase examples in the training partition. Verification candidates are balanced, and all views share canonical lineage rather than independent concepts.}}{8}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sa_mc_level_distribution}{{2}{8}{Primary-source corpus composition and training views. Panel~(a) shows 10,560 canonical records by source and reasoning level; panel~(b) shows MC/SA shares and their level composition; panel~(c) shows generation, verification, and paraphrase examples in the training partition. Verification candidates are balanced, and all views share canonical lineage rather than independent concepts}{figure.caption.6}{}}
